# Figma MCP Integration Rules — ShengRi

## Component Organization

- Admin UI components: `apps/admin/src/resources/[resource-name]/`
- Shared layout components: `apps/admin/src/layout/`
- Theme configuration: `apps/admin/src/theme.ts`
- Data providers: `apps/admin/src/dataProvider.ts`
- Auth: `apps/admin/src/authProvider.ts`

## Design Tokens

All colors, typography, and spacing are centralized in `apps/admin/src/theme.ts`.

### Color Tokens (never hardcode hex values)

| Role | Token Path | Value | Meaning |
|------|-----------|-------|---------|
| Primary | `primary.main` | #c44520 | 朱砂红 — main brand color |
| Primary Light | `primary.light` | #d86a4a | Hover / lighter accent |
| Primary Dark | `primary.dark` | #8a3016 | Pressed / gradient endpoint |
| Secondary | `secondary.main` | #dca310 | 金色 — gold highlights |
| Background | `background.default` | #fdf8f4 | Warm cream page background |
| Paper | `background.paper` | #ffffff | Card/surface background |
| Text | `text.primary` | #2d2d2d | Main text |
| Text Secondary | `text.secondary` | #666666 | Supporting text |
| Error | `error.main` | #d32f2f | Error states |
| Warning | `warning.main` | #ed6c02 | Warning states |
| Info | `info.main` | #0288d1 | Info states |
| Success | `success.main` | #2e7d32 | Success states |

### Typography

- Display/Heading font: KaiTi (楷体) family
- h5: fontWeight 700, h6: fontWeight 600
- Use MUI Typography component with variant prop

### Spacing

- Base unit: 8px (MUI default)
- Page padding: 24px (`p: 3`)
- Card internal: 16px (`p: 2`)
- Drawer width: 240px
- AppBar height: 64px

## Required Figma-to-Code Workflow (do not skip)

1. Run `get_design_context` first to fetch the structured representation for the exact node(s)
2. If the response is too large or truncated, run `get_metadata` to get the high-level node map, then re-fetch only the required node(s) with `get_design_context`
3. Run `get_screenshot` for a visual reference of the node variant being implemented
4. Only after you have both `get_design_context` and `get_screenshot`, download any assets needed and start implementation
5. Translate the output into this project's conventions: React + MUI + Emotion (`sx` prop)
6. Validate against Figma for 1:1 look and behavior before marking complete

## Implementation Rules

- IMPORTANT: Treat Figma MCP output (often React + Tailwind) as a design reference, NOT as final code
- IMPORTANT: Replace all Tailwind utility classes with MUI `sx` prop equivalents
- IMPORTANT: Reuse existing MUI components from `@mui/material` — do not create custom primitives
- IMPORTANT: Map Figma colors to theme palette tokens, never hardcode hex values
- Use react-admin components for CRUD views (List, Datagrid, SimpleForm, etc.)
- Preserve the project's KaiTi font stack for all text elements
- Use MUI Icons from `@mui/icons-material` for icon replacements
- Follow react-admin resource naming conventions

## Figma-to-MUI Translation Guide

| Figma Concept | MUI Equivalent |
|---------------|----------------|
| Auto Layout (horizontal) | `<Stack direction="row">` or `<Box sx={{ display: 'flex' }}>` |
| Auto Layout (vertical) | `<Stack>` or `<Box sx={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>` |
| Frame with padding | `<Box sx={{ p: N }}>` or `<Card sx={{ p: N }}>` |
| Fill container | `sx={{ width: '100%' }}` or `flexGrow: 1` |
| Fixed size | `sx={{ width: N, height: N }}` |
| Border radius | `sx={{ borderRadius: N }}` (N in theme units) |
| Drop shadow | `<Paper elevation={N}>` or `sx={{ boxShadow: N }}` |
| Text styles | `<Typography variant="hN/body1/body2/caption">` |
| Icons | `@mui/icons-material` equivalents |
| Buttons | `<Button variant="contained/outlined/text" color="primary/secondary">` |

## Asset Handling

- IMPORTANT: If the Figma MCP server returns a localhost source for an image or SVG, use that source directly
- IMPORTANT: DO NOT import/add new icon packages — use `@mui/icons-material`
- IMPORTANT: DO NOT use or create placeholders if a localhost source is provided
- Store downloaded assets in `apps/admin/public/assets/`

## Localization

- All user-facing text MUST be in Chinese Simplified (简体中文)
- Date format: YYYY-MM-DD or YYYY年MM月DD日
- Currency: ¥ prefix with 2 decimal places
